DeX Drive service (dex-drive-d) - what is in this folder and where it comes from

dex-drive-d      The service. MIT (LICENSE), Copyright (c) 2026 Zakhar Vityk.
                 Source: native/dex_drive/dexd in github.com/Zakh294/bmw-sugar-apps (Go, built static for x86-64:
                 tools/dex_drive/build_native.sh).

dexdec           The GPU video decoder. GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE.dexdec).
                 Source: native/dex_drive/dexdec in the same repository. Its decoder (src/decoder_msdk.*),
                 NAL reader (src/nal_reader.*), MGVF writer (src/mgvf.*) and ABI lists (abi/) are from RideTube's
                 ytdec (github.com/JustAnotherPU/ridetube), which has them from Robert Nisipeanu's waze-on-cluster
                 (github.com/robertnisipeanu/idrive-apps), GPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 2026 Robert Nisipeanu,
                 modified by JustAnotherPU and, for DeX Drive, by Zakhar Vityk (decoding order for a live stream;
                 the notices in each file say what). abi/include/mfx: Intel Media SDK headers, MIT (their LICENSE).
                 It links the head unit's own Intel Media SDK and libva at run time; nothing of them is shipped.

